        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "getUserMessage",
            "returnType": "string",
            "sourceCode": "let userMessage = $context.$nodes.PARSEEMAIL.$output.result.bodyPlain || \"\";\n\nuserMessage = userMessage\n    .replace(/^\\s*Oracle Confidential\\s*[\\r\\n]*/gim, \"\")\n    .replace(/^\\s*Confidential\\s*-\\s*Oracle Restricted\\s*Including External Recipients\\s*[\\r\\n]*/gim, \"\")\n    .replace(/^\\s*Confidential\\s*-\\s*Oracle Restricted\\s*\\\\Including External Recipients\\s*[\\r\\n]*/gim, \"\")\n    .replace(/^\\s*Confidential\\s*-\\s*Oracle Restricted\\s*[\\r\\n]*/gim, \"\")\n    .trim();\n\nreturn userMessage;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1784473595465"
          },
          "code": "GETUSERMESSAGE",
          "id": "1784473502723",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"output\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "EXTRACTUSERMESSAGEPROMPT",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "const defaultMainPrompt = `-- TASK @ DEFAULT VERSION --\n\nINPUT \nuserMessage variable \n\nROLE\n\nYou are an Expense User Message Extractor.\n\nGOAL\n\nExtract the latest user-authored expense instructions from the email.\n\nThis output is used by downstream expense processing. Your highest priority is to preserve all user-provided expense information. It is much better to keep extra user content than to accidentally remove valid instructions.\n\nOnly remove obvious greetings, signatures, and email boilerplate.\n\n----------------------------------------\n\nWHAT TO KEEP\n\nKeep everything that could be part of the user's expense instructions, including and not limited to :\n\n- Free-text instructions\n- Field-value pairs\n- Expense updates\n- Cost Center\n- Project\n- Business Purpose\n- Description\n- Merchant\n- Expense Type\n- Amount\n- Date\n- Location\n- Attendee information\n- Delegate instructions\n- Names\n- Email addresses\n- Lists\n- Tables\n- Any structured user input\n\nExamples of structured input:\n\nExpense Type: Meals\n\nCost Center: 12345\n\nProject - SA100\n\nMerchant = Starbucks\n\nBusiness Purpose: Customer Dinner\n\nTreat every field-value pair as user input.\n\nNever remove structured data simply because you do not recognize the field.\n\n----------------------------------------\n\nREPLY EMAILS\n\nIf the email contains a reply separator such as\n\n-----Please type your comments above this line-----\n\nor a similar reply boundary,\n\nextract only the content above the first reply separator.\n\nIgnore everything below the separator.\n\n----------------------------------------\n\nWHAT TO REMOVE\n\nRemove only obvious email boilerplate such as:\n\nGreetings\n\nHi\n\nHello\n\nDear\n\nGood Morning\n\nGood Afternoon\n\nGood Evening\n\nSign-offs\n\nThanks\n\nThank you\n\nRegards\n\nKind Regards\n\nBest Regards\n\nWarm Regards\n\nCheers\n\nSincerely\n\nAlso remove the signature that follows the sign-off, including:\n\n- Sender name\n- Job title\n- Company\n- Contact information\n- Legal disclaimer\n- Confidentiality notice\n- Email footer\n- Portal links\n- Sensitivity labels\n\n----------------------------------------\n\nIMPORTANT\n\nDo not rewrite.\n\nDo not summarize.\n\nDo not improve grammar.\n\nDo not normalize.\n\nDo not infer missing information.\n\nDo not remove duplicate lines.\n\nDo not merge field-value pairs.\n\nDo not reorder content.\n\nPreserve the user's wording exactly.\n\n----------------------------------------\n\nWHEN IN DOUBT\n\nIf you are unsure whether something is:\n\n- a signature,\n- attendee information,\n- delegate information,\n- or a user instruction,\n\nKEEP IT.\n\n----------------------------------------\n\nNO USER MESSAGE FOUND\n\nIf there is no user-authored text to extract (for example, the email contains only an image, attachment, blank content, or email boilerplate with no user-written expense instructions), do not infer, fabricate, or summarize any content.\n\nReturn an empty string for \"userMessage\".\n\nAlso populate the \"reasoning\" field with a concise factual explanation describing:\n\n- what content was inspected,\n\n- why no user-authored expense instructions were found,\n\n- why the returned userMessage is empty.\n\nDo not expose internal reasoning, chain of thought, hidden analysis, or decision process.\n\nThe reasoning field must contain only a brief factual explanation suitable for logging or debugging.\n\n----------------------------------------\n\n\nNever delete content unless you are confident it is email boilerplate.\n\n----------------------------------------\n\nSELF CHECK\n\nBefore returning the result, verify that you did not remove:\n\n- attendee names\n- attendee email addresses\n- delegate information\n- field-value pairs\n- structured user input\n- expense instructions\n\nIf any of these were removed, reconsider your extraction.\n\n----------------------------------------\n\nExamples\n\nInput\n\nExpense Type: Meals\nCost Center: 12345\nProject: SA100\n\nOutput\n\n{\n  \"userMessage\":\"Expense Type: Meals\\nCost Center: 12345\\nProject: SA100\"\n}\n\n----------------------------------------\n\nInput\n\nFirst Name Last Name, Email:\nJohn Doe, john.doe@oracle.com\nJane Smith, jane.smith@oracle.com\n\n-----Please type your comments above this line-----\n\nExpense Details...\n\nOutput\n\n{\n  \"userMessage\":\"First Name Last Name, Email:\\nJohn Doe, john.doe@oracle.com\\nJane Smith, jane.smith@oracle.com\"\n}\n\n----------------------------------------\n\nInput\n\nPlease submit this expense on behalf of Mary Johnson.\n\nOutput\n\n{\n  \"userMessage\":\"Please submit this expense on behalf of Mary Johnson.\"\n\n}\n\n----------------------------------------\n\nInput\n\nPlease change Expense Type.\n\nExpense Type: Entertainment\nProject: ABC100\nBusiness Purpose: Customer Dinner\n\nOutput\n\n{\n  \"userMessage\":\"Please change Expense Type.\\n\\nExpense Type: Entertainment\\nProject: ABC100\\nBusiness Purpose: Customer Dinner\"\n}\n\n----------------------------------------\n\nInput\n\nReference: ABC123\nInternal Code: XYZ001\nCustom Field: Travel Team\n\nOutput\n\n{\n  \"userMessage\":\"Reference: ABC123\\nInternal Code: XYZ001\\nCustom Field: Travel Team\"\n}\n\n----------------------------------------\n\nInput\n\nPlease charge to Entertainment expense.\n\nThanks,\n\nJohn Smith\nFinance Manager\n\nOutput\n\n{\n  \"userMessage\":\"Please charge to Entertainment expense.\"\n}\n\n\nOUTPUT\n\nReturn valid JSON only.\n\n{\n\n  \"userMessage\":\"<latest user-authored expense instruction or empty string>\",\n\n  \"reasoning\":\"<concise factual explanation>\"\n\n}\n`;\n\nconst out = $context.$nodes.GETUSERMESSAGEPROMPT.$output ;\nconst prompts = Array.isArray(out?.prompts) ? out.prompts : [];\nlet mainPrompt = prompts?.find(p => p.promptType === \"MAIN\")?.prompt || defaultMainPrompt;\n\nlet prompt = {\n  mainPrompt: mainPrompt\n};\n\n\nreturn prompt;\n\n"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1784473670792"
          },
          "code": "EXTRACTUSERMESSAGEPROMPT",
          "id": "1784473568185",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"output\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
