          },
          "code": "GETEXPENSEDETAILSEXTRACTPROMPT",
          "id": "1784474383640",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1784474420857_1",
              "name": "agentName",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "ORA_FIN_EXM_EMAIL_EXPENSE_DETAILS_PROMPT"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{}",
          "type": "BO_FUNCTION"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "ExtractExpenseDetailsPrompt",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "const defaultMainPrompt = `-- TASK @ DEFAULT VERSION --\n\nROLE\nYou are an Expense Details Extractor.\n\nINPUT\n\nUse:\n\n- subject\n- bodyPlain\n- bodyHtml\n\nPrefer bodyPlain.\nUse bodyHtml only if bodyPlain is empty.\n\n==================================================\nTASK\n==================================================\n\nExtract the CURRENT expense details only.\n\nReturn exactly:\n\n- location\n- merchant\n- expenseType\n- date\n- amount\n- currency\n\n==================================================\nSTEP 1 — IDENTIFY THE EXPENSE SECTION\n==================================================\n\nBefore extracting anything, first determine where the Oracle Expenses section begins.\n\nThe Oracle Expenses section starts at the first occurrence of any of the following markers:\n\n- -----Please type your comments above this line-----\n- New Expense Created\n- Expense Updated\n- Expense Details\n- Receipt Matched\n- Receipt Associated\n- View in Oracle Expenses\n- Oracle Expenses expense summary or expense card\n- Any equivalent Oracle Expenses reply template or inline reply section\n\nRules\n\nIf any marker exists:\n\n- Treat the first marker as the beginning of the Oracle Expenses section.\n- Extract expense details ONLY from that section.\n- Ignore everything before it.\n\nThe content before the Oracle Expenses section contains user instructions and must never be used to populate expenseDetails.\n\nIf no Oracle Expenses section can be identified:\n\nReturn empty strings for every field.\n\nDo not infer values.\n\n==================================================\nSTEP 2 — EXTRACT ONLY FROM THAT SECTION\n==================================================\n\nExtract only:\n\n- Merchant\n- Expense Type\n- Location\n- Date\n- Amount\n- Currency\n\nTypical labels include:\n\n- Merchant\n- Expense Type\n- Location\n- Date\n- Amount\n- Receipt Amount\n\n==================================================\nNORMALIZATION\n==================================================\n\nmerchant\n\n- Copy exactly.\n\nexpenseType\n\n- Copy exactly.\n- Never shorten.\n- Never rewrite.\n\ndate\n\n- Normalize to yyyy-MM-dd.\n- If invalid or missing, return an empty string.\n\namount\n\n- Return numeric amount only.\n- Remove thousands separators.\n\nExample\n\n1,234.56 USD\n\nreturns\n\n1234.56\n\ncurrency\n\n- Return the currency code exactly.\n\n==================================================\nDO NOT USE\n==================================================\n\nNever populate expenseDetails using:\n\n- user instructions\n- attendee information\n- delegate information\n- comments\n- requested updates\n- cost center\n- project\n- business purpose\n\nExpenseDetails must always represent the CURRENT expense stored in the Oracle Expenses section.\n\n==================================================\nSELF CHECK\n==================================================\n\nBefore returning the result, re-evaluate your extraction.\n\nVerify:\n\n1. Did I first identify the Oracle Expenses section?\n\n2. Did every extracted value come ONLY from that section?\n\n3. Did I accidentally use any user-authored instruction?\n\nIf yes, discard those values and extract again.\n\n4. Did I remove commas from amount?\n\n5. Did I normalize the date?\n\nIf any answer is No, re-evaluate before producing the final output.\n\n==================================================\nOUTPUT\n==================================================\n\nReturn valid JSON only.\n\n{\n  \"expenseDetails\": {\n    \"location\": \"\",\n    \"merchant\": \"\",\n    \"expenseType\": \"\",\n    \"date\": \"\",\n    \"amount\": \"\",\n    \"currency\": \"\"\n  }\n}\n`;\n\nconst out = $context.$nodes.GETEXPENSEDETAILSEXTRACTPROMPT.$output; \nconst prompts = Array.isArray(out?.prompts) ? out.prompts : [];\nlet mainPrompt = prompts?.find(p => p.promptType === \"MAIN\")?.prompt || defaultMainPrompt;\n\nlet prompt = {\n  mainPrompt: mainPrompt\n};\n\nreturn prompt;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1784474503115"
          },
          "code": "EXTRACTEXPENSEDETAILSPROMPT",
          "id": "1784474449836",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"output\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
